BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 636.8 Tm (\(3 rows\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 604.8 Tm (Why Interviewers Ask This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 579.6 Tm (Almost every SQL bug a candidate will hit - alias errors, WHERE vs HAVING confusion,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 566.1 Tm (LIMIT picking the wrong rows, aggregates in the wrong clause - is explained by this one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 552.6 Tm (list. If you know the order, you can derive the rules instead of memorising them.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 523.1 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 497.9 Tm (- Reciting the order but not being able to use it to explain the alias error.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 484.8 Tm (- Believing the database physically executes in this order \(it does not; the optimiser is free) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 471.7 Tm (to reorder as long as results match\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 458.2 Tm (- Putting a row filter in HAVING where WHERE belongs - it works but filters late and costs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 445.1 Tm (performance.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 415.6 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 390.4 Tm (- Push filters as early as possible: row conditions in WHERE, group conditions in HAVING.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 377.3 Tm (- Use a CTE when an expression is needed in both SELECT and WHERE - name it once.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 364.2 Tm (- Remember LIMIT is last: LIMIT 10 without ORDER BY returns an arbitrary 10 rows.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 335.1 Tm (Follow-up Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 309.9 Tm (1. Where do window functions fit in this order? \(After HAVING, alongside SELECT - which is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 296.8 Tm (why you cannot filter on a window function in WHERE.\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 283.3 Tm (2. Why can you GROUP BY an ordinal position \(GROUP BY 1\) but not always by alias?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 270.2 Tm (3. If the optimiser can reorder, why does the logical order matter at all?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 257.1 Tm (4. Does LIMIT without ORDER BY ever return a stable result set?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 228.0 Tm (Real-world Scenario) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 202.8 Tm (A reporting endpoint paginated with LIMIT 20 OFFSET 40 and no ORDER BY. It worked for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 189.3 Tm (months on a small table where Postgres happened to return rows in physical order. After a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 175.8 Tm (VACUUM FULL rewrote the heap, page 3 started showing rows that had already appeared on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 162.3 Tm (page 1. The bug was never in the pagination code - it was the missing final-step sort.) Tj ET
