BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 167.3 Tm (Why does WHERE city = NULL return no rows? Explain SQL's three-valued logic.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 137.8 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 112.6 Tm (NULL is not a value - it is a marker meaning "unknown". Comparing anything to an unknown) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 99.1 Tm (yields UNKNOWN, not TRUE or FALSE. SQL therefore has three-valued logic:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 85.6 Tm (TRUE, FALSE, UNKNOWN.) Tj ET
