BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 728.0 Tm (WHERE keeps a row only when the predicate is exactly TRUE. city = NULL evaluates to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 714.5 Tm (UNKNOWN, so the row is discarded - which is why the query returns zero rows instead of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 701.0 Tm ("the rows with no city". The correct operators are IS NULL and IS NOT NULL.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 682.5 Tm (Truth tables worth memorising:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 659.0 Tm (A        B        A AND B  A OR B) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 648.8 Tm (---------------------------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 638.5 Tm (TRUE     UNKNOWN  UNKNOWN  TRUE) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 628.2 Tm (FALSE    UNKNOWN  FALSE    UNKNOWN) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 618.0 Tm (UNKNOWN  UNKNOWN  UNKNOWN  UNKNOWN) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 595.8 Tm (Consequences that show up in real bugs:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 577.2 Tm (- NULL = NULL is UNKNOWN, but NULL IS NOT DISTINCT FROM NULL is TRUE.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 564.2 Tm (- NOT \(city = 'Mumbai'\) does not include NULL cities.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 551.1 Tm (- city NOT IN \('Mumbai', NULL\) returns no rows ever - the NULL poisons the whole list.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 538.0 Tm (- NULL in arithmetic propagates: 1000 * NULL is NULL.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 524.9 Tm (- But UNIQUE constraints and GROUP BY treat NULLs as equal to each other, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 511.8 Tm (ORDER BY sorts them together. The rules are deliberately inconsistent across features.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 482.3 Tm (Example) Tj ET
