BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 543.4 Tm (NULL handling is the highest-density source of silent data corruption in SQL. A candidate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 529.9 Tm (who explains three-valued logic and then predicts the NOT IN behaviour is demonstrating that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 516.4 Tm (they debug from a model rather than by trial and error.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 486.9 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 461.7 Tm (- Using = NULL or != NULL.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 448.6 Tm (- Assuming NOT IN with a subquery is safe - if the subquery can yield a single NULL, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 435.5 Tm (outer query returns nothing. This is the classic "my anti-join returns zero rows" bug.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 422.0 Tm (- Thinking NULL and empty string '' are the same. They are not \(except in Oracle\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 408.9 Tm (- Believing NULL never counts as a duplicate - GROUP BY groups all NULLs together.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 379.8 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 354.6 Tm (- Prefer NOT EXISTS over NOT IN for anti-joins - it is NULL-safe and usually plans better.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 341.5 Tm (- Declare columns NOT NULL DEFAULT ... unless "unknown" is a genuine business state.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 328.4 Tm (- Make the meaning of NULL explicit in the schema comment: unknown, not-applicable, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 315.3 Tm (not-yet-known are three different things.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 301.8 Tm (- In ORDER BY, state NULLS FIRST or NULLS LAST rather than relying on engine defaults.) Tj ET
