BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 712.0 Tm (Question 6) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 679.8 Tm (Difficulty: Easy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 666.2 Tm (Category: SQL -> COALESCE, NULLIF) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 636.8 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 611.5 Tm (What do COALESCE and NULLIF do? How do you use them together to avoid division by zero?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 582.0 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 556.8 Tm (COALESCE\(a, b, c, ...\) returns the first non-NULL argument, evaluated left to right, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 543.3 Tm (short-circuits. It is the ANSI-standard way to supply a default. Engine-specific cousins:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 529.8 Tm (ISNULL \(SQL Server, two args only\), IFNULL \(MySQL\), NVL \(Oracle\). Prefer COALESCE -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 516.3 Tm (it is portable and takes any number of arguments.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 497.8 Tm (NULLIF\(a, b\) returns NULL if a = b, otherwise returns a. It is the inverse tool:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 484.3 Tm (it creates a NULL deliberately.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 465.8 Tm (The idiom x / NULLIF\(y, 0\) is the standard division-by-zero guard: when y is 0 the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 452.3 Tm (denominator becomes NULL, so the whole expression is NULL instead of raising) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 438.8 Tm (division by zero. Wrap it in COALESCE to present 0 to the caller:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 415.3 Tm (COALESCE\(x / NULLIF\(y, 0\), 0\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 394.3 Tm (This is safer than a CASE WHEN y = 0 guard because it cannot be defeated by the optimiser) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 380.8 Tm (evaluating branches in an unexpected order.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 351.3 Tm (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 326.1 Tm (Compute the effective total per order \(discount is often NULL\), and a stock turnover ratio) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 312.6 Tm (where stock_qty can legitimately be 0 \(ProBook 15\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 283.1 Tm (Code Example) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 252.9 Tm (-- 1. COALESCE supplies a default for a NULL discount) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 242.9 Tm (SELECT o.order_id,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 232.9 Tm (       o.discount_pct                              AS raw_discount,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 222.9 Tm (       COALESCE\(o.discount_pct, 0\)                 AS effective_discount,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 212.9 Tm (       SUM\(oi.quantity * oi.unit_price\)            AS gross,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 202.9 Tm (       ROUND\(SUM\(oi.quantity * oi.unit_price\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 192.9 Tm (             * \(1 - COALESCE\(o.discount_pct, 0\) / 100\), 2\) AS net_payable) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 182.9 Tm (FROM   orders o) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 172.9 Tm (JOIN   order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 162.9 Tm (GROUP  BY o.order_id, o.discount_pct) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 152.9 Tm (ORDER  BY o.order_id;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 135.5 Tm (-- 2. NULLIF prevents division by zero for the zero-stock product) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 125.5 Tm (SELECT p.name,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 115.5 Tm (       p.stock_qty,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 105.5 Tm (       SUM\(oi.quantity\)                                        AS units_sold,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 95.5 Tm (       ROUND\(SUM\(oi.quantity\)::numeric / NULLIF\(p.stock_qty, 0\), 2\) AS turnover,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 85.5 Tm (       COALESCE\(ROUND\(SUM\(oi.quantity\)::numeric) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 75.5 Tm (                      / NULLIF\(p.stock_qty, 0\), 2\), 0\)         AS turnover_safe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 276.9 32 Tm 0.45 g (Page 16 of 160) Tj ET 0 g
endstream
