BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 436.6 Tm (Explain the CASE expression. What is the difference between the simple and searched forms?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 407.1 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 381.9 Tm (CASE is SQL's conditional expression - it returns a value, so it can appear anywhere a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 368.4 Tm (value can: SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, GROUP BY, even inside an aggregate. It is not a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 354.9 Tm (statement and has no side effects.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 336.4 Tm (Searched form - each branch has a full predicate. Most flexible; use this by default.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 312.9 Tm (CASE WHEN qty = 0 THEN 'out of stock') Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 302.9 Tm (     WHEN qty < 10 THEN 'low') Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 292.9 Tm (     ELSE 'healthy' END) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 271.9 Tm (Simple form - one expression compared for equality against constants. Shorter, but only) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 258.4 Tm (tests =, and it cannot test NULL \(because NULL = NULL is UNKNOWN\).) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 234.9 Tm (CASE status WHEN 'PENDING' THEN 1 WHEN 'SHIPPED' THEN 2 ELSE 9 END) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 213.8 Tm (Key semantics:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 195.3 Tm (- Branches are evaluated top to bottom and the first TRUE wins - order matters, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 182.3 Tm (overlapping conditions are silently shadowed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 168.8 Tm (- Omitting ELSE implies ELSE NULL. This is the single most common CASE bug.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 155.7 Tm (- All result branches must share a compatible type; the engine determines one result type.) Tj ET
