BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 403.5 Tm (WITH RECURSIVE has exactly two parts joined by UNION ALL:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 380.0 Tm (WITH RECURSIVE t AS \() Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 370.0 Tm (    <anchor member>            -- runs once, seeds the result) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 360.0 Tm (    UNION ALL) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 349.9 Tm (    <recursive member>         -- references t, runs repeatedly) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 339.9 Tm (\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 318.9 Tm (Execution model:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 300.4 Tm (1. Evaluate the anchor -> put rows in the working table.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 287.3 Tm (2. Evaluate the recursive member using only the rows produced by the previous iteration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 274.2 Tm (3. Append those rows to the result and make them the new working table.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 261.2 Tm (4. Repeat until an iteration produces zero rows. That is the termination condition.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 243.1 Tm (So recursion stops naturally when no child rows match - not because of a counter. If the data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 229.6 Tm (contains a cycle \(A is a parent of B, B is a parent of A\) it never terminates. Two defences:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 211.1 Tm (- A depth guard: WHERE depth < 10.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 198.0 Tm (- A path array with WHERE NOT node = ANY\(path\) to detect revisits.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 179.9 Tm (Note UNION ALL versus UNION: UNION de-duplicates each iteration, which masks cycles but is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 166.4 Tm (much slower. Use UNION ALL plus an explicit cycle guard.) Tj ET
