BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 717.0 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 691.8 Tm (- Index for your actual query patterns, verified with EXPLAIN ANALYZE and pg_stat_statements.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 678.7 Tm (- Put the equality column first in a composite index, the range or sort column second.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 665.6 Tm (- Use partial indexes for skewed data - the "open orders" case is often 1 percent of the table.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 652.5 Tm (- Create indexes with CONCURRENTLY in production to avoid write locks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 639.4 Tm (- Audit and drop unused indexes on a schedule.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 610.3 Tm (Follow-up Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 585.1 Tm (1. Why does \(customer_id, order_date\) not help WHERE order_date = ??) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 572.0 Tm (2. What is a covering index and how do you confirm an index-only scan?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 558.9 Tm (3. When would a hash, GIN or BRIN index beat a B-tree?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 545.8 Tm (4. What is index bloat and how does REINDEX CONCURRENTLY help?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 532.7 Tm (5. How do indexes interact with NULL values?) Tj ET
