BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 436.3 Tm (Why Interviewers Ask This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 411.1 Tm (ACID is the vocabulary of data correctness, and the interviewer wants to know whether you write) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 397.6 Tm (BEGIN/COMMIT deliberately or rely on autocommit and hope. The WHERE stock_qty >= 1 guard) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 384.1 Tm (is the detail that shows you have thought about two users buying the last item simultaneously.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 354.6 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 329.4 Tm (- Reciting the acronym without being able to name a bug each property prevents.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 316.3 Tm (- Reading stock, checking it in application code, then updating - a race condition. Do the check) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 303.2 Tm (in the WHERE clause or lock the row with SELECT ... FOR UPDATE.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 289.7 Tm (- No ROLLBACK in the error path, leaving the transaction open and holding locks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 276.7 Tm (- Not releasing the connection in finally - connection pool exhaustion under load.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 263.6 Tm (- Long transactions spanning user think-time or external HTTP calls.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 234.5 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 209.3 Tm (- Keep transactions short: no network calls, no user interaction inside them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 196.2 Tm (- Push invariants into the schema \(CHECK \(stock_qty >= 0\)\) so a logic bug cannot violate them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 183.1 Tm (- Make retries safe with an idempotency key so a client retry does not double-charge.) Tj ET
