BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 576.7 Tm (Question 19) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 544.5 Tm (Difficulty: Hard) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 531.0 Tm (Category: SQL -> Isolation levels) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 501.5 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 476.3 Tm (Name the four SQL isolation levels and the anomalies each prevents. Which does PostgreSQL use by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 462.8 Tm (default, and how does it differ from the standard?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 433.3 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 408.1 Tm (Isolation controls what one transaction can see of another's uncommitted or concurrent work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 394.6 Tm (Weaker isolation means more concurrency and more anomalies.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 376.1 Tm (The anomalies:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 357.6 Tm (- Dirty read - reading another transaction's uncommitted data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 344.5 Tm (- Non-repeatable read - re-reading the same row and getting a different value because) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 331.4 Tm (someone else committed an UPDATE in between.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 317.9 Tm (- Phantom read - re-running the same range query and finding new rows that another) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 304.8 Tm (transaction inserted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 291.3 Tm (- Lost update - two transactions read, both write, the second overwrites the first.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 278.2 Tm (- Write skew - both transactions read an overlapping set, each makes a decision that is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 265.1 Tm (individually valid, and the combination violates an invariant. Only SERIALIZABLE prevents it.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 241.6 Tm (Level             Dirty read  Non-repeatable read  Phantom                  Write skew) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 231.3 Tm (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 221.1 Tm (READ UNCOMMITTED  possible    possible             possible                 possible) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 210.8 Tm (READ COMMITTED    prevented   possible             possible                 possible) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 200.6 Tm (REPEATABLE READ   prevented   prevented            possible \(per standard\)  possible) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 190.3 Tm (SERIALIZABLE      prevented   prevented            prevented                prevented) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 168.1 Tm (Engine reality, which is what interviews actually reward:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 149.6 Tm (- PostgreSQL default is READ COMMITTED. Every statement sees a fresh snapshot.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 136.5 Tm (READ UNCOMMITTED is accepted but behaves as READ COMMITTED - Postgres cannot do dirty) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 123.0 Tm (reads at all, because MVCC never exposes uncommitted tuples. Postgres REPEATABLE READ is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 109.5 Tm (snapshot isolation and does prevent phantoms, which is stricter than the standard requires.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 96.0 Tm (SERIALIZABLE uses Serializable Snapshot Isolation \(SSI\) and can abort with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 82.5 Tm (ERROR: could not serialize access - applications must retry.) Tj ET
