BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 717.0 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 691.8 Tm (- Believing an ORM makes you immune. Raw-SQL escape hatches \(query, raw, whereRaw,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 678.7 Tm (@Query with string concatenation\) reintroduce the hole.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 665.2 Tm (- Escaping quotes manually or stripping keywords with a blocklist.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 652.1 Tm (- Trying to parameterise a table or column name and then falling back to concatenation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 639.0 Tm (- Forgetting second-order injection: stored input reused later to build SQL.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 625.9 Tm (- Running the app as the database owner, so a successful injection is catastrophic rather than) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 612.8 Tm (merely bad.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 583.3 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 558.1 Tm (- Parameterise everything; make string-concatenated SQL a lint error in CI.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 545.0 Tm (- Allow-list identifiers for dynamic ORDER BY and dynamic table names.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 531.9 Tm (- Grant the application role the minimum privileges; separate migration and runtime roles.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 518.8 Tm (- Never store passwords with reversible or fast hashes - use Argon2id or bcrypt.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 505.7 Tm (- Add a static analysis / SAST rule and a dependency scan; log and alert on query errors that) Tj ET
