BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 728.0 Tm (Isolation defaults - Postgres READ COMMITTED \(no dirty reads ever; REPEATABLE READ also) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 714.5 Tm (blocks phantoms; SERIALIZABLE needs retry on SQLSTATE 40001\). MySQL InnoDB REPEATABLE READ) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 701.0 Tm (with gap locks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 682.5 Tm (Injection - parameterise values, allow-list identifiers, least privilege. An ORM is not a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 669.0 Tm (guarantee.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 650.5 Tm (Common misconceptions cleared) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 632.0 Tm (1. "CTEs are always slower in Postgres" - false since version 12; single-reference CTEs inline.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 618.9 Tm (2. "SELECT COUNT\(1\) is faster than COUNT\(*\)" - identical plans.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 605.8 Tm (3. "Indexes only help" - they tax every write and can be ignored by the planner.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 592.7 Tm (4. "READ UNCOMMITTED gives dirty reads in Postgres" - it does not; MVCC forbids it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 579.6 Tm (5. "HAVING and WHERE are interchangeable" - only accidentally, for non-aggregate predicates.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 566.5 Tm (6. "An ORM prevents SQL injection" - only until the first raw call.) Tj ET
