BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 483.5 Tm (Question 24) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 451.3 Tm (Difficulty: Medium) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 437.8 Tm (Category: SQL -> Views, materialised views) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 408.3 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 383.1 Tm (What is a view? How does a materialised view differ, and when do you use each?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 353.6 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 328.4 Tm (A view is a stored query. It holds no data; every reference re-executes the underlying SQL.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 314.9 Tm (Benefits: encapsulation, a stable interface over a changing schema, and column-level security.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 301.4 Tm (Cost: no performance gain whatsoever - it is a macro.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 282.9 Tm (A materialised view stores the result on disk. Reads are as fast as a table \(and it can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 269.4 Tm (indexed\), but the data is a snapshot that goes stale until refreshed.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 245.9 Tm (               View                                    Materialised view) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 235.6 Tm (------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 225.4 Tm (Stores data    no                                      yes) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 215.1 Tm (Read cost      cost of the query                       cost of a table scan or index lookup) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 204.9 Tm (Freshness      always current                          stale until refreshed) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 194.6 Tm (Indexable      no                                      yes) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 184.4 Tm (Write-through  sometimes \(simple views are updatable\)  never) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 162.1 Tm (REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW takes an exclusive lock and blocks readers;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 148.6 Tm (REFRESH ... CONCURRENTLY does not, but requires a UNIQUE index and does more work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 130.1 Tm (Use a view for abstraction and permissioning. Use a materialised view when an expensive) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 116.6 Tm (aggregate is read far more often than the data changes, and minutes of staleness are acceptable.) Tj ET
