BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 728.0 Tm (by long transactions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 709.5 Tm (Prevention, in order of effectiveness:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 691.0 Tm (1. Always acquire locks in a deterministic order - for example ascending primary key. If) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 677.9 Tm (every transaction locks row 1 before row 2, no cycle can form.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 664.4 Tm (2. Keep transactions short - less overlap, less contention.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 651.3 Tm (3. Use a single atomic statement where possible; one statement cannot deadlock with itself.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 638.2 Tm (4. Retry on 40P01 with jitter - deadlocks are a normal, expected condition at scale.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 625.1 Tm (5. SELECT ... FOR UPDATE NOWAIT or SKIP LOCKED for queue workloads.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 596.0 Tm (Example) Tj ET
