BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 614.8 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 589.5 Tm (Explain 1NF, 2NF, 3NF and BCNF with a single worked example. When would you denormalise?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 560.0 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 534.8 Tm (Normalisation removes redundancy so that each fact is stored once, eliminating update) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 521.3 Tm (anomalies.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 502.8 Tm (- 1NF - atomic values, no repeating groups. No comma-separated lists in a column.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 489.8 Tm (- 2NF - 1NF plus: no partial dependency. Every non-key column depends on the whole) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 476.7 Tm (composite key, not part of it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 463.2 Tm (- 3NF - 2NF plus: no transitive dependency. Non-key columns must not depend on other) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 450.1 Tm (non-key columns.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 436.6 Tm (- BCNF - stricter 3NF: every determinant is a candidate key. Fixes the rare case where a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 423.5 Tm (non-key column determines part of a key.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 405.0 Tm (Mnemonic: 1NF kills repeating groups, 2NF kills partial dependencies, 3NF kills) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 391.5 Tm (transitive dependencies, BCNF kills the leftovers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 373.0 Tm (Denormalise deliberately when read performance demands it: precomputed totals, duplicated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 359.5 Tm (display names to avoid a join, or a reporting star schema. The price is that you now own) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 346.0 Tm (consistency - every copy must be updated together, usually by trigger, application logic, or a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 332.5 Tm (scheduled reconciliation job. Denormalise for measured read pressure, never for convenience.) Tj ET
