BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 717.0 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 686.8 Tm (                         Function                 Procedure                Trigger) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 676.5 Tm (----------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 666.3 Tm (Returns a value          yes, required            optional \(OUT/INOUT\)     no \(returns NULL or NEW\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 656.0 Tm (Callable in SELECT       yes                      no - use CALL            never called directly) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 645.8 Tm (Can manage transactions  no \(runs inside caller~  yes - COMMIT/ROLLBACK ~  no) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 635.5 Tm (Invocation               explicit                 explicit                 implicit, by DML) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 625.3 Tm (Typical use              reusable calculation     multi-step batch job     audit, derived column, ~) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 603.0 Tm (PostgreSQL gained true PROCEDURE support with transaction control in version 11; before that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 589.5 Tm (everything was a function.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 571.0 Tm (Triggers are powerful and easy to misuse. They are the right tool for audit trails and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 557.5 Tm (enforcing invariants that must hold regardless of which code path writes. They are the wrong) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 544.0 Tm (tool when:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 525.5 Tm (- Business logic hides in them - debugging becomes archaeology, since nothing in the application) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 512.5 Tm (code shows the effect.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 499.0 Tm (- They cascade: trigger A writes a table with trigger B, which writes back. Recursion and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 485.9 Tm (surprise performance cliffs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 472.4 Tm (- They do heavy work per row on bulk loads - a COPY of a million rows fires a million times.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 459.3 Tm (- They perform external side effects such as notifications; a rollback cannot un-send an email.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 441.2 Tm (FOR EACH STATEMENT triggers avoid the per-row cost when you only need one action per DML.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 411.7 Tm (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 386.5 Tm (An audit trigger recording every status change, and a function computing an order total.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 357.0 Tm (Code Example) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 326.8 Tm (-- ============ FUNCTION: reusable, callable in SELECT ============) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 316.8 Tm (CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION order_total\(p_order_id INT\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 306.8 Tm (RETURNS NUMERIC) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 296.8 Tm (LANGUAGE sql) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 286.8 Tm (STABLE                                  -- no writes; planner can optimise) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 276.7 Tm (AS $$) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 266.7 Tm (    SELECT COALESCE\(SUM\(quantity * unit_price\), 0\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 256.7 Tm (    FROM   order_items WHERE order_id = p_order_id;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 246.7 Tm ($$;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 229.4 Tm (SELECT order_id, order_total\(order_id\) AS total FROM orders ORDER BY order_id LIMIT 3;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 212.0 Tm (-- ============ PROCEDURE: multi-step, owns its transactions ============) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 202.0 Tm (CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE cancel_stale_orders\(p_days INT\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 192.0 Tm (LANGUAGE plpgsql) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 182.0 Tm (AS $$) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 172.0 Tm (DECLARE) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 161.9 Tm (    v_count INT;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 151.9 Tm (BEGIN) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 141.9 Tm (    UPDATE orders) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 131.9 Tm (    SET    status = 'CANCELLED') Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 121.9 Tm (    WHERE  status = 'PENDING') Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 111.9 Tm (      AND  order_date < CURRENT_DATE - p_days;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 101.9 Tm (    GET DIAGNOSTICS v_count = ROW_COUNT;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 84.5 Tm (    RAISE NOTICE 'cancelled % stale orders', v_count;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 74.5 Tm (    COMMIT;                             -- legal in a procedure, not in a function) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 276.9 32 Tm 0.45 g (Page 73 of 160) Tj ET 0 g
endstream
