BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 284.0 Tm ( order_id | old_status | new_status) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 274.0 Tm (----------+------------+------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 264.0 Tm (        5 | PENDING    | SHIPPED) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 232.0 Tm (Why Interviewers Ask This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 206.8 Tm (It probes where you believe business logic belongs. Both extremes are wrong answers: "everything) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 193.3 Tm (in the database" and "never use a trigger". The mature answer distinguishes invariants and audit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 179.8 Tm (\(database\) from workflow \(application\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 150.3 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 125.1 Tm (- Trying to COMMIT inside a function.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 112.0 Tm (- Using FOR EACH ROW where FOR EACH STATEMENT suffices, then wondering why bulk inserts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 98.9 Tm (crawl.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 85.4 Tm (- Returning NULL from a BEFORE trigger by accident, silently cancelling the write.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 72.3 Tm (- Sending emails or calling HTTP from a trigger, which cannot be rolled back.) Tj ET
