BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 501.1 Tm (5. Security risk of SECURITY DEFINER without a fixed search_path?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 472.1 Tm (Real-world Scenario) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 446.9 Tm (An order table had a trigger that recalculated a customer summary row on every insert. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 433.4 Tm (marketing backfill inserted 3 million historical orders; the trigger fired 3 million times, each) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 419.9 Tm (one locking the same summary row, and the import ran for nine hours before being killed. The fix) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 406.4 Tm (was a statement-level trigger plus a nightly recompute, dropping the import to four minutes.) Tj ET
0.6 w 0.65 G 54 381.9 m 558 381.9 l S 0 G
BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 349.9 Tm (Question 30) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 317.6 Tm (Difficulty: Medium) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 304.1 Tm (Category: SQL -> GROUP BY advanced) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 274.6 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 249.4 Tm (What are GROUPING SETS, ROLLUP and CUBE? How do you tell a subtotal row from a real NULL?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 219.9 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 194.7 Tm (These produce multiple levels of aggregation in one pass instead of UNION ALL-ing several) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 181.2 Tm (queries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 162.7 Tm (- GROUPING SETS \(\(a,b\),\(a\),\(\)\) - explicitly list the groupings you want.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 149.6 Tm (- ROLLUP\(a, b\) - hierarchical subtotals: \(a,b\), \(a\), \(\). Use for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 136.5 Tm (year -> month -> day or country -> city.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 123.0 Tm (- CUBE\(a, b\) - every combination: \(a,b\), \(a\), \(b\), \(\). 2^n groupings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 104.9 Tm (Subtotal rows carry NULL in the columns not being grouped, which is ambiguous when the data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 91.4 Tm (itself contains NULLs. The GROUPING\(col\) function disambiguates: it returns 1 when the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 77.9 Tm (column was aggregated away in that row, 0 when it is a real value. Combine it with CASE to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 276.9 32 Tm 0.45 g (Page 75 of 160) Tj ET 0 g
