stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 728.0 Tm (produce readable labels.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 698.5 Tm (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 673.3 Tm (Revenue by country and city with automatic city subtotals and a grand total. Sara Khan's NULL) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 659.8 Tm (city is exactly the ambiguity this feature creates.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 630.3 Tm (Code Example) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 600.1 Tm (SELECT COALESCE\(c.country, '\(all countries\)'\)                    AS country,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 590.1 Tm (       CASE WHEN GROUPING\(c.city\) = 1 THEN '\(all cities\)') Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 580.1 Tm (            ELSE COALESCE\(c.city, '\(unknown city\)'\)              -- real NULL, distinguished) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 570.1 Tm (       END                                                       AS city,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 560.1 Tm (       COUNT\(DISTINCT o.order_id\)                                AS orders,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 550.1 Tm (       COALESCE\(SUM\(oi.quantity * oi.unit_price\), 0\)             AS revenue,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 540.1 Tm (       GROUPING\(c.country\) AS g_country,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 530.1 Tm (       GROUPING\(c.city\)    AS g_city) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 520.1 Tm (FROM       customers   c) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 510.1 Tm (LEFT  JOIN orders      o  ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id AND o.status <> 'CANCELLED') Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 500.1 Tm (LEFT  JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id   = o.order_id) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 490.1 Tm (GROUP BY   ROLLUP \(c.country, c.city\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 480.1 Tm (ORDER BY   g_country, country, g_city, city;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 462.7 Tm (-- CUBE: also gives per-city totals across all countries) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 452.7 Tm (-- GROUP BY CUBE \(c.country, c.city\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 435.3 Tm (-- Equivalent to ROLLUP but explicit) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 425.3 Tm (-- GROUP BY GROUPING SETS \(\(c.country, c.city\), \(c.country\), \(\)\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 393.3 Tm (Output) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 363.1 Tm (    country      |     city      | orders |  revenue  | g_country | g_city) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 353.1 Tm (-----------------+---------------+--------+-----------+-----------+--------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 343.1 Tm ( India           | Bengaluru     |      3 | 197493.00 |         0 |      0) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 333.1 Tm ( India           | Chennai       |      1 |   4999.00 |         0 |      0) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 323.1 Tm ( India           | Delhi         |      0 |      0.00 |         0 |      0) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 313.1 Tm ( India           | Mumbai        |      2 |  13997.00 |         0 |      0) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 303.0 Tm ( India           | \(all cities\)  |      6 | 216489.00 |         0 |      1) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 293.0 Tm ( UAE             | \(unknown city\)|      0 |      0.00 |         0 |      0) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 283.0 Tm ( UAE             | \(all cities\)  |      0 |      0.00 |         0 |      1) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 273.0 Tm ( USA             | Austin        |      1 |  16497.00 |         0 |      0) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 263.0 Tm ( USA             | \(all cities\)  |      1 |  16497.00 |         0 |      1) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 253.0 Tm ( \(all countries\) | \(all cities\)  |      7 | 232986.00 |         1 |      1) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 243.0 Tm (\(10 rows\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 222.0 Tm (The UAE rows show why GROUPING matters: \(unknown city\) is Sara's genuine NULL, while) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 208.5 Tm (\(all cities\) is the subtotal. Without GROUPING both would print as NULL and be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 195.0 Tm (indistinguishable.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 165.5 Tm (Why Interviewers Ask This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 140.3 Tm (It is a reporting-heavy question that separates candidates who would UNION ALL three queries) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 126.8 Tm (from those who know the single-pass feature. The GROUPING disambiguation is the detail that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 113.3 Tm (shows real usage.) Tj ET
