BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 717.0 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 691.8 Tm (- Using UNION ALL of three aggregate queries, scanning the table three times.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 678.7 Tm (- Assuming a NULL in the output is always a subtotal marker.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 665.6 Tm (- Expecting CUBE to be cheap - it computes 2^n groupings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 652.5 Tm (- Sorting without accounting for subtotal rows, so totals land in the middle of the report.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 623.4 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 598.2 Tm (- ROLLUP for hierarchies, GROUPING SETS when you need specific combinations only, CUBE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 585.1 Tm (rarely and on low-cardinality columns.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 571.6 Tm (- Always label subtotals with GROUPING\(...\) rather than exposing raw NULLs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 558.5 Tm (- Order by the GROUPING flags so totals appear last.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 529.4 Tm (Follow-up Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 504.2 Tm (1. How many grouping sets does CUBE\(a, b, c\) produce? \(Eight.\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 491.1 Tm (2. What does GROUPING_ID give you over GROUPING?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 478.0 Tm (3. How would you achieve the same with window functions instead?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 464.9 Tm (4. Which is cheaper for one subtotal level: ROLLUP or a window SUM OVER \(\)?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 435.9 Tm (Real-world Scenario) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 410.7 Tm (A finance export ran four separate aggregate queries - by region, by country, by city, and a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 397.2 Tm (grand total - then stitched them in Python. Each scanned a 90-million-row fact table. A single) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 383.7 Tm (ROLLUP query replaced all four, cut the export from 11 minutes to 90 seconds, and removed the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 370.2 Tm (class of bug where the four scans saw slightly different data.) Tj ET
0.6 w 0.65 G 54 345.7 m 558 345.7 l S 0 G
BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 313.7 Tm (Revision Notes: SQL Questions 21-30) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 276.4 Tm (Topic               One-line takeaway) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 266.2 Tm (-------------------------------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 255.9 Tm (Keys                super key \(any unique set\) -> candidate \(minimal\) -> primary \(chosen one\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 245.7 Tm (UNION vs UNION ALL  ALL is the default choice; UNION pays for a dedupe sort) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 235.4 Tm (Pagination          OFFSET is O\(m+n\) and unstable; keyset is O\(log n\) and stable) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 225.2 Tm (Views               a view is a macro, not a cache; materialised views store rows and go stale) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 214.9 Tm (Deadlocks           caused by inconsistent lock order; fix by ordering, then retry on 40P01) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 204.7 Tm (Normalisation       1NF atomic, 2NF no partial, 3NF no transitive, BCNF every determinant a key) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 194.4 Tm (EXPLAIN             compare estimated vs actual rows first; that gap is usually the root cause) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 184.2 Tm (Partitioning        one server, prune by key; sharding is many servers, much more expensive) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 173.9 Tm (Triggers            audit and invariants yes, business workflow no, per-row on bulk loads never) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 163.7 Tm (ROLLUP              one pass for subtotals; use GROUPING\(\) to label them) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 141.4 Tm (Sargable predicates - keep the column bare on the left:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 117.9 Tm (BAD : WHERE EXTRACT\(YEAR FROM order_date\) = 2025) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 107.9 Tm (GOOD: WHERE order_date >= '2025-01-01' AND order_date < '2026-01-01') Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 97.9 Tm (BAD : WHERE UPPER\(email\) = 'A@B.COM') Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 87.9 Tm (GOOD: WHERE email = 'a@b.com'          -- with a LOWER\(\) expression index if needed) Tj ET
