BT /F2 22 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 608.0 Tm (SECTION 2: MERN STACK) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 559.3 Tm (Numbering restarts per section. These are MERN Q1 onward.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 524.8 Tm (MERN Q1) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 492.5 Tm (Difficulty: Easy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 479.0 Tm (Category: MongoDB -> Fundamentals) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 449.5 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 424.3 Tm (How does MongoDB's document model differ from a relational model? When would you choose each?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 394.8 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 369.6 Tm (MongoDB stores BSON documents in collections. There is no enforced schema by default, arrays) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 356.1 Tm (and nested objects are first-class, and related data is often embedded rather than joined.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 332.6 Tm (               Relational                         MongoDB) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 322.4 Tm (---------------------------------------------------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 312.1 Tm (Unit           row in a table                     document in a collection) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 301.9 Tm (Schema         enforced by DDL                    flexible; optional JSON Schema validation) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 291.6 Tm (Relationships  foreign keys + joins               embedding, or references + $lookup) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 281.4 Tm (Transactions   ACID, always multi-row             ACID, multi-document since 4.0 \(replica set requi~) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 271.1 Tm (Scaling        vertical, then read replicas       horizontal sharding built in) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 260.9 Tm (Best at        complex joins, strong constraints  hierarchical documents, high write throughput, ev~) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 238.6 Tm (The real decision rule is access pattern, not preference. Embed when data is read together) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 225.1 Tm (and bounded in size \("one product's reviews on the product page"\). Reference when data is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 211.6 Tm (shared,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 198.1 Tm (unbounded, or updated independently \("users referenced by orders"\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 179.6 Tm (The 16 MB document limit is a hard design constraint: any array that grows without bound - audit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 166.1 Tm (logs, chat messages, follower lists - must be its own collection.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 136.6 Tm (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 111.4 Tm (An e-commerce order: line items are embedded \(always read with the order, bounded\), while the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 97.9 Tm (customer is referenced \(shared across many orders, updated independently\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 276.9 32 Tm 0.45 g (Page 79 of 160) Tj ET 0 g
