BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 488.5 Tm (Aggregation is the differentiator between "I can do CRUD" and "I can build features". Stage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 475.0 Tm (ordering is a direct performance question with a verifiable answer.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 445.5 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 420.3 Tm (- Putting $match after $group or $unwind, losing all index use.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 407.2 Tm (- $unwind-ing a large array when $map plus $sum would compute the same value in place.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 394.2 Tm (- $lookup before reducing the document count, so the join runs per raw document.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 381.1 Tm (- Forgetting preserveNullAndEmptyArrays on $unwind after $lookup, silently dropping) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 368.0 Tm (documents with no match - the MongoDB equivalent of turning a LEFT JOIN into an INNER JOIN.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 354.5 Tm (- Ignoring the 100 MB stage limit on big pipelines.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 325.4 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 300.2 Tm (- $match first, $sort next, $project away unused fields early to shrink documents.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 287.1 Tm (- Verify with db.coll.explain\("executionStats"\).aggregate\([...]\) and look for IXSCAN.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 274.0 Tm (- Prefer $addFields with array operators over $unwind + $group round trips.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 260.9 Tm (- Use $facet when a page needs results plus a count in one round trip.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 231.8 Tm (Follow-up Questions) Tj ET
