BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 690.0 Tm (MERN Q3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 657.8 Tm (Difficulty: Medium) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 644.2 Tm (Category: MongoDB -> Indexes) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 614.8 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 589.5 Tm (How do MongoDB indexes work? Explain the ESR rule for compound indexes.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 560.0 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 534.8 Tm (MongoDB uses B-tree indexes much like relational engines. Every collection has an index on _id.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 521.3 Tm (Types: single-field, compound, multikey \(automatic on array fields\), text, geospatial,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 507.8 Tm (hashed, wildcard, plus partial and TTL variants.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 489.3 Tm (ESR rule - order compound index keys as Equality, Sort, Range:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 465.8 Tm ({ status: 1,        // E - equality match) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 455.8 Tm (  orderDate: -1,    // S - sort field) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 445.8 Tm (  total: 1 }        // R - range filter) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 424.8 Tm (Reason: equality narrows to a contiguous region, the sort field then already has the right order) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 411.3 Tm (\(no in-memory sort\), and range scanning last still reads a contiguous span. Putting the range) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 397.8 Tm (before the sort forces a blocking sort.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 379.3 Tm (Like SQL composite indexes, MongoDB obeys the prefix rule: {a:1, b:1, c:1} serves queries on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 365.8 Tm (a, a+b, a+b+c, but not b alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 347.3 Tm (A covered query is answered from the index alone - requires that all returned fields are in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 333.8 Tm (the index and _id is excluded from the projection.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 304.3 Tm (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 279.1 Tm (Order history screen: filter by status, sort newest first, optional minimum total.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 249.6 Tm (Code Example) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 219.4 Tm (// ESR-ordered compound index) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 209.4 Tm (db.orders.createIndex\({ status: 1, orderDate: -1, total: 1 },) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 199.4 Tm (                      { name: "status_date_total" }\);) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 182.0 Tm (// Uses the index fully: equality + sort + range) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 172.0 Tm (db.orders.find\({ status: "DELIVERED", total: { $gte: 10000 } }\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 162.0 Tm (         .sort\({ orderDate: -1 }\).limit\(20\);) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 144.7 Tm (// Partial index: index only the small hot subset) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 134.6 Tm (db.orders.createIndex\() Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 124.6 Tm (  { orderDate: -1 },) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 114.6 Tm (  { partialFilterExpression: { status: { $in: ["PENDING", "SHIPPED"] } },) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 104.6 Tm (    name: "open_orders_date" }) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 94.6 Tm (\);) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 77.2 Tm (// Unique index \(the equivalent of a UNIQUE constraint\)) Tj ET
