BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 374.0 Tm (  executionStats: { nReturned: 20, totalDocsExamined: 480000,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 364.0 Tm (                    executionTimeMillis: 1120 } }) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 343.0 Tm (The tell-tale ratio is totalDocsExamined versus nReturned. Close to 1:1 is healthy;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 329.5 Tm (480000:20 means a collection scan.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 300.0 Tm (Why Interviewers Ask This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 274.8 Tm (Indexing is the top MongoDB performance topic, and ESR is a concrete, memorable rule that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 261.3 Tm (candidates either know or do not.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 231.8 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 206.6 Tm (- Creating one single-field index per query field instead of one well-ordered compound index.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 193.5 Tm (- Ignoring sort direction: {a:1, b:-1} does not serve sort\({a:1, b:1}\) efficiently.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 180.4 Tm (- Assuming an index on an array field behaves like a scalar index \(multikey has restrictions -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 167.3 Tm (you cannot have a compound index on two array fields\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 153.8 Tm (- Believing indexes are free; each one taxes every write and consumes RAM in the working set.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 140.8 Tm (- Not checking $indexStats before adding yet another index.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 111.7 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 86.5 Tm (- Order compound keys by ESR and verify with explain\("executionStats"\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 73.4 Tm (- Watch totalDocsExamined / nReturned; investigate anything far above 1.) Tj ET
