BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 728.0 Tm (including your own write.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 709.5 Tm (Multi-document transactions \(4.0 replica sets, 4.2 sharded clusters\) give ACID across) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 696.0 Tm (documents and collections. Single-document writes are already atomic, so a transaction is only) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 682.5 Tm (needed when two or more documents must change together and you cannot restructure to embed them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 669.0 Tm (They cost more than single writes and hold locks, so prefer schema design that avoids them.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 639.5 Tm (Example) Tj ET
