BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 491.6 Tm (Why Interviewers Ask This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 466.4 Tm (This is the MongoDB distributed-systems question. It tests whether you understand the durability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 452.9 Tm (and consistency knobs rather than accepting defaults, and whether you know that transactions are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 439.4 Tm (a last resort in a document database, not the primary tool.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 409.9 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 384.7 Tm (- Saying MongoDB is not ACID. It is, per document always, and across documents since 4.0.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 371.6 Tm (- Using w: 1 for financial writes, then losing acknowledged data on failover.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 358.5 Tm (- Reading from secondaries and being surprised by stale data - then "fixing" it with retries) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 345.4 Tm (instead of causal consistency or primary reads.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 331.9 Tm (- Wrapping every operation in a transaction, hurting throughput for no benefit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 318.8 Tm (- Not handling TransientTransactionError; withTransaction does it for you, manual code does) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 305.7 Tm (not.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 292.2 Tm (- Leaking sessions by skipping endSession.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 263.1 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 237.9 Tm (- w: "majority" plus readConcern: "majority" for anything you cannot lose.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 224.8 Tm (- Prefer single-document atomicity by embedding what must change together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 211.7 Tm (- Keep transactions under a second and touching few documents; default limit is 60 seconds.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 198.6 Tm (- Use causalConsistency sessions for read-your-own-write on secondary reads.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 185.6 Tm (- Monitor replication lag and alert on it, since it silently changes read semantics.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 156.5 Tm (Follow-up Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 131.3 Tm (1. How does the oplog work, and what happens when a secondary falls off the end of it?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 118.2 Tm (2. What is a rollback and how does readConcern: majority protect you?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 105.1 Tm (3. Why is an arbiter usually a bad idea for a three-node set?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 92.0 Tm (4. How do transactions behave on a sharded cluster differently?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 78.9 Tm (5. What is the difference between readConcern and readPreference?) Tj ET
