BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 631.2 Tm (Why Interviewers Ask This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 606.0 Tm (Middleware is the core Express abstraction; nearly every Express question reduces to it. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 592.5 Tm (four-argument error handler and the async-error gap are the details that reveal real experience.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 563.0 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 537.8 Tm (- Registering the error handler before the routes, so it never fires.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 524.7 Tm (- Writing \(err, req, res\) with three parameters - Express treats it as normal middleware.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 511.6 Tm (- Forgetting next\(\), producing a request that hangs with no error.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 498.5 Tm (- Calling next\(\) and sending a response, causing "Cannot set headers after they are sent".) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 485.4 Tm (- Assuming async handler rejections reach the error handler in Express 4.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 472.3 Tm (- Leaking err.stack to the client in production.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 443.2 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 418.0 Tm (- Fixed order: correlation id, logging, security headers, body parsing, routes, 404, error) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 405.0 Tm (handler.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 391.5 Tm (- Wrap async handlers or move to Express 5.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 378.4 Tm (- Set body size limits; never accept unbounded JSON.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 365.3 Tm (- Attach a request id and include it in both logs and error responses for support.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 352.2 Tm (- Keep middleware single-purpose and testable in isolation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 323.1 Tm (Follow-up Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 297.9 Tm (1. How does Express distinguish an error handler from normal middleware?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 284.8 Tm (2. What happens if two middleware both write to the response?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 271.7 Tm (3. app.use versus router.use versus route-level arrays - when each?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 258.6 Tm (4. How do you make one middleware run only for certain HTTP methods?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 245.5 Tm (5. What changed for async errors in Express 5?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 216.4 Tm (Real-world Scenario) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 191.2 Tm (An API returned HTTP 200 with an empty body under load. A validation middleware called) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 177.7 Tm (next\(err\) and also wrote a response; the error handler then tried to write again and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 164.2 Tm (double-write was swallowed. Adding a rule that middleware either responds or calls next, never) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 150.7 Tm (both, plus a lint rule, ended a week of intermittent debugging.) Tj ET
