BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 712.0 Tm (MERN Q6) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 679.8 Tm (Difficulty: Medium) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 666.2 Tm (Category: Express -> Authentication, JWT) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 636.8 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 611.5 Tm (How does JWT authentication work? Compare it with sessions and describe secure token storage.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 582.0 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 556.8 Tm (A JWT is three base64url segments: header.payload.signature. The server signs the payload;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 543.3 Tm (any party with the key can verify it without a database lookup. That statelessness is the entire) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 529.8 Tm (value proposition - and the entire problem, because a valid token cannot be un-issued.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 506.3 Tm (                    Session \(server state\)            JWT \(stateless\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 496.1 Tm (---------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 485.8 Tm (Storage             server store \(Redis\) + cookie id  client holds the token) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 475.6 Tm (Revocation          delete the session - immediate    impossible without a blocklist) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 465.3 Tm (Scaling             needs shared store                none needed) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 455.1 Tm (Payload visibility  opaque id                         readable by anyone \(signed, not encrypted\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 444.8 Tm (Size per request    small cookie                      larger header) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 422.6 Tm (The standard production pattern is a pair of tokens:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 404.1 Tm (- Access token - JWT, short lived \(5 to 15 minutes\), sent on every request.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 391.0 Tm (- Refresh token - long lived, stored server-side so it can be revoked, used only to mint) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 377.9 Tm (new access tokens, and rotated on each use so a stolen token is detectable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 359.4 Tm (Storage: keep the refresh token in an httpOnly, Secure, SameSite cookie so JavaScript) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 345.9 Tm (cannot read it \(XSS protection\). localStorage is readable by any injected script. Cookies need) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 332.4 Tm (CSRF defence: SameSite=Strict or Lax plus a CSRF token for state-changing requests.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 313.9 Tm (A JWT payload is signed, not encrypted - never put secrets in it.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 284.4 Tm (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 259.2 Tm (Login issues both tokens; a middleware verifies the access token; refresh rotates.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 229.7 Tm (Code Example) Tj ET
