BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 499.0 Tm (Why Interviewers Ask This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 473.8 Tm (Auth is where security mistakes are most expensive. They are checking whether you know JWTs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 460.3 Tm (cannot be revoked, why localStorage is risky, and whether you have implemented refresh) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 446.8 Tm (rotation - the difference between tutorial auth and production auth.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 417.3 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 392.1 Tm (- Long-lived access tokens \(days\) with no refresh mechanism - a stolen token stays valid.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 379.0 Tm (- Storing tokens in localStorage, so any XSS is a full account takeover.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 365.9 Tm (- Putting sensitive data in the payload, believing it is encrypted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 352.8 Tm (- Accepting the alg from the token header, enabling alg: none or algorithm-confusion attacks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 339.7 Tm (- Storing refresh tokens in plaintext in the database.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 326.6 Tm (- Hashing passwords with SHA-256 or MD5 instead of Argon2id or bcrypt.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 313.5 Tm (- No issuer/audience validation, so a token from another service is accepted.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 284.4 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 259.2 Tm (- Short access token, rotating refresh token stored hashed, revocable server-side.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 246.1 Tm (- Refresh token in an httpOnly, Secure, SameSite cookie scoped to the refresh path only.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 233.0 Tm (- Pin the algorithm explicitly on verify; validate iss and aud.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 219.9 Tm (- Detect refresh reuse and revoke the entire token family - that is a theft signal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 206.8 Tm (- Argon2id for passwords; rate-limit login; never reveal whether an email exists.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 177.7 Tm (Follow-up Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 152.5 Tm (1. How do you revoke a JWT before it expires?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 139.4 Tm (2. Why is httpOnly insufficient without CSRF protection?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 126.4 Tm (3. What is refresh token rotation and what attack does it detect?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 113.3 Tm (4. Symmetric HS256 versus asymmetric RS256 - when does each fit?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 100.2 Tm (5. How would you handle logout across five devices?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 276.9 32 Tm 0.45 g (Page 94 of 160) Tj ET 0 g
