BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 501.0 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 475.8 Tm (Why is React state immutable, and what happens if you mutate it directly?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 446.3 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 421.1 Tm (React decides whether to re-render by comparing the reference of the previous and next state) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 407.6 Tm (\(Object.is\). Mutating an object or array in place keeps the same reference, so React sees no) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 394.1 Tm (change and skips the render - the UI silently goes stale. Immutability also makes state) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 380.6 Tm (transitions traceable and lets React.memo, useMemo and useCallback compare cheaply.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 362.1 Tm (State updates are also asynchronous and batched. Calling setCount\(count + 1\) three times in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 348.6 Tm (one handler stales on the same count; the updater form setCount\(c => c + 1\) reads the latest) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 335.1 Tm (value each time.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 305.6 Tm (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 280.4 Tm (A cart where adding an item with push fails to render but the spread form works.) Tj ET
