BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 417.6 Tm (variant is the follow-up that separates memorisation from understanding.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 388.1 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 362.9 Tm (- push, splice, sort, reverse or direct property assignment on state.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 349.8 Tm (- Passing the current value instead of an updater when the next value depends on the previous.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 336.8 Tm (- Deep-cloning everything with JSON.parse\(JSON.stringify\(...\)\) - slow and drops Date,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 323.7 Tm (undefined and Map.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 310.2 Tm (- Using array index as key, which breaks identity when the list reorders.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 281.1 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 255.9 Tm (- Spread or array methods that return new values: map, filter, concat, toSorted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 242.8 Tm (- Always use the updater form when deriving from previous state.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 229.7 Tm (- Reach for useReducer once updates involve several interdependent fields.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 216.6 Tm (- Immer \(or Redux Toolkit, which bundles it\) for deeply nested state.) Tj ET
