BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 494.3 Tm (condition?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 464.8 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 439.6 Tm (useEffect\(fn, deps\) runs a side effect after render and commit. The dependency array) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 426.1 Tm (controls re-execution:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 402.6 Tm (deps     Runs) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 392.4 Tm (-------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 382.1 Tm (omitted  after every render) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 371.9 Tm ([]       once after mount \(twice in dev Strict Mode\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 361.6 Tm ([a, b]   on mount and whenever a or b change by Object.is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 339.4 Tm (The returned function is cleanup: it runs before the next effect execution and on unmount.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 325.9 Tm (That is where you abort requests, clear timers and close sockets.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 307.4 Tm (Data fetching has two hazards. First, race conditions: two in-flight requests can resolve out) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 293.9 Tm (of order, so a stale response overwrites a fresh one. Second, leaks: setting state after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 280.4 Tm (unmount. Both are solved with AbortController plus an ignore flag in cleanup.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 261.9 Tm (React 18 Strict Mode intentionally mounts, unmounts and remounts effects in development to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 248.4 Tm (expose) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 234.9 Tm (missing cleanup. That is a feature, not a bug.) Tj ET
