0.6 w 0.65 G 54 413.0 m 558 413.0 l S 0 G
BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 381.0 Tm (MERN Q9) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 348.8 Tm (Difficulty: Medium) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 335.3 Tm (Category: React -> useMemo, useCallback, memo) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 305.8 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 280.6 Tm (When should you use useMemo, useCallback and React.memo? When are they harmful?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 251.1 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 225.9 Tm (All three are referential-stability tools, not general speed-ups.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 207.4 Tm (- useMemo\(fn, deps\) caches a computed value between renders.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 194.3 Tm (- useCallback\(fn, deps\) caches a function identity between renders.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 181.2 Tm (- React.memo\(Component\) skips re-rendering when props are shallow-equal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 163.1 Tm (They are worth it when \(a\) a computation is genuinely expensive, or \(b\) a value or function is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 149.6 Tm (passed to a memo-ised child or used in another hook's dependency array. Without one of those,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 136.1 Tm (you pay the cost of the comparison plus retained memory for nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 117.6 Tm (Critical interaction: React.memo is defeated by any new reference in props. Passing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 104.1 Tm (onClick={\(\) => ...} or style={{...}} creates a new value each render, so the child always) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 90.6 Tm (re-renders and memo is pure overhead. That is why useCallback and memo are usually adopted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 77.1 Tm (together or not at all.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 276.9 32 Tm 0.45 g (Page 99 of 160) Tj ET 0 g
