BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 221.3 Tm (The Virtual DOM is a lightweight JavaScript tree describing the intended UI. On state change,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 207.8 Tm (React builds a new tree and diffs it against the previous one \(reconciliation\), then applies) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 194.3 Tm (the minimal set of real DOM mutations. DOM writes are the expensive part; diffing plain objects) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 180.8 Tm (is cheap by comparison.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 162.3 Tm (React's diff uses two heuristics to stay O\(n\) instead of O\(n^3\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 143.8 Tm (1. Different element type means discard the subtree. <div> to <span> unmounts everything) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 130.7 Tm (inside, losing child state.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 117.2 Tm (2. Keys identify children across renders. Within a list, React matches elements by key, not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 104.1 Tm (by position.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 85.6 Tm (That is why index keys are dangerous: if you prepend or reorder, index 0 now refers to a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 72.1 Tm (different item, so React reuses the wrong DOM node and its state - the classic symptom is a) Tj ET
