BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 728.0 Tm (So the ordering is: **synchronous code, then all nextTick, then all promise microtasks, then) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 714.5 Tm (timers, then I/O, then setImmediate**. setImmediate runs in the check phase - after I/O -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 701.0 Tm (despite the name, whereas setTimeout\(fn, 0\) runs in the timers phase of the next iteration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 682.5 Tm (Consequence: any CPU-bound synchronous work blocks the whole loop, and therefore every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 669.0 Tm (concurrent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 655.5 Tm (request. That is what worker_threads exists to solve.) Tj ET
