BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 582.3 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 557.1 Tm (- Believing Node is multithreaded for JavaScript, or that it is single-threaded for everything) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 544.0 Tm (\(file I/O and crypto use the thread pool\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 530.5 Tm (- Saying setImmediate runs before setTimeout\(fn, 0\) always - it depends on the current phase.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 517.4 Tm (- Forgetting process.nextTick outranks promises, and that a recursive nextTick can starve the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 504.3 Tm (loop entirely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 490.8 Tm (- Using Sync APIs \(readFileSync, pbkdf2Sync\) in a request path.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 477.7 Tm (- Assuming worker_threads helps with I/O - it is for CPU work.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 448.6 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 423.4 Tm (- Never run CPU-bound work on the main thread; use worker_threads or a separate service.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 410.3 Tm (- Prefer async APIs; reserve Sync variants for startup code.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 397.2 Tm (- Watch event loop lag as a first-class metric \(perf_hooks.monitorEventLoopDelay\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 384.1 Tm (- Use setImmediate to yield between chunks when processing large arrays.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 371.0 Tm (- Size UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE when heavy on file or crypto operations.) Tj ET
