BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 507.8 Tm (What is a closure? Give a practical use and a memory-leak risk.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 478.3 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 453.1 Tm (A closure is a function bundled with the lexical environment it was created in. The inner) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 439.6 Tm (function keeps its outer variables alive after the outer function returns, because it still) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 426.1 Tm (references them. That is the mechanism behind data privacy, function factories, memoisation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 412.6 Tm (once, debounce and throttle, and module state.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 394.1 Tm (The leak risk is the flip side: as long as the closure is reachable, everything it captures is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 380.6 Tm (retained - including large arrays or DOM nodes captured accidentally.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 351.1 Tm (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 325.9 Tm (A private counter, a rate limiter, and a memoiser.) Tj ET
