BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 478.3 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 453.1 Tm (For normal functions, this is decided at call time by these rules, in priority order:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 434.6 Tm (1. new Foo\(\) - this is the new instance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 421.6 Tm (2. Explicit binding - fn.call\(obj\), fn.apply\(obj\), fn.bind\(obj\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 408.5 Tm (3. Implicit binding - obj.fn\(\), this is obj.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 395.4 Tm (4. Default - undefined in strict mode / modules, globalThis otherwise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 377.3 Tm (Arrow functions have no own this. They capture it lexically from the enclosing scope and it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 363.8 Tm (cannot be reassigned - bind, call and apply cannot change it. That is why arrows are correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 350.3 Tm (for callbacks and wrong for object methods that need the receiver, and for prototype methods.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 326.8 Tm (             call        apply  bind) Tj ET
