BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 494.3 Tm (Explain the browser event loop, the call stack, macrotasks and microtasks. Predict the output.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 464.8 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 439.6 Tm (JavaScript has one call stack. The event loop repeatedly: takes one macrotask from the task) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 426.1 Tm (queue, runs it to completion, then drains the entire microtask queue, then lets the browser) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 412.6 Tm (render if needed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 394.1 Tm (- Macrotasks: setTimeout, setInterval, DOM events, network callbacks,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 381.1 Tm (MessageChannel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 367.6 Tm (- Microtasks: promise callbacks, queueMicrotask, MutationObserver.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 349.5 Tm (The critical asymmetry: all pending microtasks run before the next macrotask, and microtasks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 336.0 Tm (queued by microtasks are also drained in the same pass. An infinite microtask chain therefore) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 322.5 Tm (freezes the page permanently, while an infinite setTimeout chain does not.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 304.0 Tm (await x is sugar for x.then\(continuation\), so code after await is a microtask.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 290.5 Tm (requestAnimationFrame runs before paint, after microtasks.) Tj ET
