BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 207.2 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 182.0 Tm (Every object has an internal [[Prototype]] link. Property lookup walks that chain until found or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 168.5 Tm (until null. Object.getPrototypeOf\(obj\) reads it; the legacy accessor is proto.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 150.0 Tm (For a constructor F, new F\(\) creates an object whose prototype is F.prototype. Methods live) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 136.5 Tm (on F.prototype, shared by all instances - that is the memory win over per-instance functions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 118.0 Tm (class is syntactic sugar over this: it creates a constructor function, puts methods on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 104.5 Tm (prototype, and wires extends by setting the prototype chain. Differences from functions: class) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 91.0 Tm (bodies are strict mode, not hoisted for use before definition, methods are non-enumerable, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 77.5 Tm (the) Tj ET
