BT /F2 22 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 608.0 Tm (SECTION 16: OPERATING SYSTEMS) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 543.3 Tm (OS Q1) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 511.0 Tm (Difficulty: Easy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 497.5 Tm (Category: OS -> Process vs thread) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 468.0 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 442.8 Tm (Difference between a process and a thread? What is a context switch?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 413.3 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 388.1 Tm (A process is an executing program with its own virtual address space, file descriptors and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 374.6 Tm (resources. A thread is a unit of execution inside a process; threads share the heap, code and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 361.1 Tm (descriptors but each has its own stack, registers and program counter.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 337.6 Tm (                Process                             Thread) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 327.4 Tm (----------------------------------------------------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 317.1 Tm (Memory          isolated                            shared heap, own stack) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 306.9 Tm (Creation cost   high \(page tables, PCB\)             low) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 296.6 Tm (Crash impact    contained                           can take down the process) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 286.4 Tm (Communication   IPC: pipes, sockets, shared memory  shared variables \(needs synchronisation\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 276.1 Tm (Context switch  expensive \(TLB and cache flush\)     cheaper \(same address space\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 253.9 Tm (A context switch saves the current execution state \(registers, program counter, stack pointer\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 240.4 Tm (and restores another's. Direct cost is a few microseconds; the indirect cost - cold CPU caches) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 226.9 Tm (and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 213.4 Tm (TLB misses - is usually larger. Excessive switching is thrashing, visible as high system CPU) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 199.9 Tm (with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 186.4 Tm (low throughput.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 156.9 Tm (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 131.7 Tm (A browser uses one process per tab for isolation, and threads inside each tab for rendering,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 118.2 Tm (networking and compositing.) Tj ET
