BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 199.6 Tm (compact demonstration of understanding.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 170.1 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 144.9 Tm (- Saying threads have separate memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 131.8 Tm (- Believing more threads always means more throughput - beyond core count, switching dominates.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 118.7 Tm (- Not recognising counter++ as three operations \(load, add, store\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 105.6 Tm (- Confusing concurrency \(interleaved progress\) with parallelism \(simultaneous execution\).) Tj ET
