BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 728.0 Tm (    the three-phase pattern - add nullable, backfill in batches, then add the constraint) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 718.0 Tm (    with NOT VALID and validate separately. I also added a rule to our migration checklist) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 708.0 Tm (    that any DDL on a table over a million rows needs a timing test against a) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 698.0 Tm (    production-sized snapshot, and I set a lock_timeout so a migration fails fast instead) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 688.0 Tm (    of queueing behind traffic. That checklist item has caught two similar migrations since,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 678.0 Tm (    including one from a senior engineer.") Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 646.0 Tm (Output) Tj ET
